<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Michael Manley</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1924">1924</a>–<a href="/years/1997">1997</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Michael Manley was Prime Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> from 1972 to 1980 and from 1989 to 1992, and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-national-party">People's National Party</a> founded by his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norman-manley">Norman Manley</a>. In his first term he pursued democratic socialism, raised the levy on bauxite and drew close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, amid economic crisis and political violence. In his second term he adopted market-oriented policies.</p></div>
